  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nWe propose a convex optimization approach inspired by optimal transport and Fourier analysis to minimize the overlap integral for the Erd\u0151s problem. The key insight is that the overlap integral can be related to the convolution of h with itself, enabling the use of spectral techniques and duality principles.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\nDefine h: [0,2] \u2192 [0,1], \u222bh(x)dx=1. The overlap integral is C\u2085 = max_k \u222bh(x)(1\u2212h(x+k))dx. Using Fourier transforms, express the problem in frequency domain and formulate a dual optimization problem with constraints \u222bh=1, h\u22650.\n\n3. Implementation procedure\na) Discretize h into n=100 points.\nb) Compute the Fourier transform of h.\nc) Formulate and solve the dual problem using CVXPY with the dual variables and constraints.\nd) Reconstruct h from the dual solution, ensuring feasibility.\n\n4. Search choices\nStart with n=100. Use CVXPY with MOSEK solver. Initialize from `initial_h_values` if available; otherwise, use a blocky function.\n\n5. Compute budget\nEstimated runtime: 600s with CVXPY and MOSEK.\n\n6. Validation\nEnsure \u2211h=50 (for n=100), 0 \u2264 h \u22641. Evalute C\u2085 using np.correlate.",
